        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70691,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are solid or cystic tumours with a haemorrhagic cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70692,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 167,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours consist of polygonal, columnar, or hobnail cells with clear cytoplasm and show a solid, tubulocystic, or papillary architecture. Nuclear atypia is mild to moderate; the mitotic count may be low. By immunohistochemistry, the tumours are positive for CK7, EMA, PAX8, and AR, and negative for WT1, CA19-9, CK20, calretinin, D2-40, ER, and PR {30921621}. Despite a low mitotic count, the Ki-67 index is high {30921621}. The differential diagnosis includes mesothelioma (positive for calretinin and D2-40) {16295392}; serous carcinoma (more pronounced cellular budding and more frequent psammoma bodies) {8653294}; and metastatic renal cell carcinoma, particularly with clear cell morphology {11469344; 32190396; 16512598}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T15:36:03"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
